# Minimal Emojis in AI-Generated Content

AI-generated posts and content should use emojis sparingly. The tone is clear, confident, and professional — not playful or salesy.

## Rules:
- Maximum 1-2 emojis per post, if any
- Never start a post with an emoji
- Never use multiple emojis in a row (e.g., 🔥🚀✨)
- Emojis should add meaning, not decoration
- When in doubt, leave the emoji out

## Acceptable uses:
- A single emoji to reinforce a CTA (e.g., "Book your spot today 📅")
- A relevant emoji to set context (e.g., "New menu dropping Friday 🍽️")

## Where this applies:
- All LLM prompts that generate user-facing posts in content_planner.py
- Single post generation in brain.py
- Any AI-generated captions, calendars, or content output

## Note:
This applies to AI-generated post OUTPUT only — not to the Gridly app UI, which has its own intentional emoji branding system (⚡📅📋📊🎯💡✨).
